<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan gold imports down 12.3 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan gold imports down 12.3 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in January fell by 12.3 percent from a year earlier to 11.50 tonnes, Ministry of Finance (MOF) data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  Jan 97     Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p> Total		  11.50	8.09	13.12</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Australia	     2.25	1.48	 5.38</p>
<p> South Africa	  3.16	1.57	 2.10</p>
<p> Britain		 0.50	1.00	 1.00</p>
<p> Canada		  0.43	0.60	 0.94</p>
<p> South Korea	   1.30	0.30	 0.60</p>
<p> Switzerland	   1.38	2.00	 1.49</p>
<p>Gold imports in 1996 totalled 134.39 tonnes, down nearly 50 percent from 262.30 tonnes in the previous year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431</p>
</text>
